===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*skey-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|schit}}, {{m|enm|schyt}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*sċite|t=dung}} and {{m|ang|sċitte|t=diarrhoea}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*skiti}} and {{m|gmw-pro|*skittjā}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*skitiz}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*skeyd-|t=to split, divide, separate}}. Related to {{cog|stq|Skiete}}, {{cog|fy|skyte}}, {{m|fy|skyt}}, {{cog|nl|schijt}}, {{cog|nds-de|Schiet}}, {{cog|de|Scheiße}}, {{cog|da|skidt}}, {{cog|sv|-}} and {{cog|nn|skit}}, {{cog|nb|skitt}}, {{cog|is|skítur}}. Compare {{m|en|shite}}. {{doublet|en|scheisse}}.

